# Character twists of Hahn series; point transport along fixing automorphisms

Definition: `HahnSeries_Monodromy` (`6d32962d-7068-5001-a021-41e07293fd91`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Let $R$ be a commutative ring. For a character $\chi \colon \mathrm{Multiplicative}\,\mathbb{Q} \to
R^{\times}$, [`HahnSeries.hahnTwistFun`](../def/HahnSeries_Monodromy.html#L10) sends a Hahn series
$x$ with value group $\mathbb{Q}$ to the series whose coefficient in degree $a \in \mathbb{Q}$ is
$\chi(a)\,x_a$; since the multipliers are units, the support is unchanged and remains partially
well-ordered. [`HahnSeries.hahnTwist`](../def/HahnSeries_Monodromy.html#L35) packages this as an
$R$-algebra automorphism of `HahnSeries ℚ R` (relative to the power-series algebra structure), with
inverse the twist by $\chi^{-1}$; multiplicativity comes from $\chi(a+b)=\chi(a)\chi(b)$ on the
antidiagonal, and $\chi(0)=1$ gives compatibility with the algebra map. A lemma layer records the
coefficients, the action on a monomial $\mathrm{single}\ a\ r \mapsto \mathrm{single}\ a\
(\chi(a)r)$, and the invariance of the support and of the order.
[`HahnSeries.hahnTwistHom`](../def/HahnSeries_Monodromy.html#L102) is the resulting monoid
homomorphism from the character group to the group of $R$-algebra automorphisms.
[`HahnSeries.MonoChar R`](../def/HahnSeries_Monodromy.html#L95) is the subgroup of characters
normalised by $\chi(1)=1$, i.e. the kernel of evaluation at the element $1 \in \mathbb{Q}$, and
[`HahnSeries.monodromy R`](../def/HahnSeries_Monodromy.html#L121) is its image under `hahnTwistHom`;
consequently every element of `monodromy R` fixes the monomial $\mathrm{single}\ 1\ 1$.

The second part concerns a Weierstrass curve $E$ over a field $K$ which is an algebra over a field
$k$, together with an automorphism $\sigma \in \mathrm{Aut}_k(K)$ satisfying $E^{\sigma} = E$, i.e.
the coefficientwise image of $E$ under $\sigma$ is $E$ itself. Then $\sigma$ preserves nonsingular
affine solutions, and
[`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.fixedTransport`](../def/HahnSeries_Monodromy.html#L199) is the
induced additive automorphism of the group of affine points: it fixes the point at infinity and
sends $(x,y)$ to $(\sigma x, \sigma y)$. Additivity rests on the compatibility of $\mathrm{negY}$,
the slope and the addition formulas with $\sigma$ under the invariance hypothesis, with the case
distinction of the chord–tangent law handled through the auxiliary declarations.

**Relation to Mathlib.** Hahn series with their power-series algebra structure, and the affine point
group of a Weierstrass curve together with the behaviour of the addition formulas under a ring
homomorphism, are Mathlib's; the character twist, the normalised character subgroup and the
monodromy subgroup are the project's own, as is the transport of points along an automorphism fixing
the curve (Mathlib's point maps go along a base change of the curve rather than from invariance of a
fixed curve).

**Where it is used.** These constructions supply, on the one hand, a group of automorphisms of
fractional-power expansions that acts trivially on the distinguished monomial of degree $1$, and on
the other hand the action of a field automorphism fixing a Weierstrass curve on its group of affine
points; both are used by later modules of the development.

